## 15. Creating an MSI with WiX Toolset

WiX is suitable for source-controlled and repeatable enterprise packaging.

### 15.1 Prerequisites

Install the approved WiX Toolset version on the build machine. Keep the WiX source files in the `installer` folder.

### 15.2 MSI design requirements

The WiX project should:

- Install `SAPTicketAssistant.exe` under Program Files
- Create a Start menu shortcut
- Optionally create a desktop shortcut
- Register the product for uninstallation
- Use a stable upgrade code across all versions
- Use a new product version for each release
- Define major-upgrade behavior
- Remove created shortcuts during uninstallation
- Avoid deleting user-generated ticket evidence unless explicitly required and approved

### 15.3 Example WiX source

The exact syntax depends on the WiX version. The following example illustrates the intended structure and should be reviewed against the WiX version approved by your organization.

```xml
<Wix xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs">
  <Package
      Name="SAP Ticket Checklist Assistant"
      Manufacturer="Your Organization"
      Version="1.0.0"
      UpgradeCode="PUT-A-STABLE-GUID-HERE"
      Language="1033"
      Scope="perMachine">

    <MajorUpgrade DowngradeErrorMessage="A newer version is already installed." />

    <StandardDirectory Id="ProgramFiles64Folder">
      <Directory Id="INSTALLFOLDER" Name="SAP Ticket Assistant">
        <Component Id="MainExecutable" Guid="*">
          <File
              Id="SAPTicketAssistantExe"
              Source="..\dist\SAPTicketAssistant.exe"
              KeyPath="yes" />
        </Component>
      </Directory>
    </StandardDirectory>

    <StandardDirectory Id="ProgramMenuFolder">
      <Directory Id="ApplicationProgramsFolder" Name="SAP Ticket Assistant">
        <Component Id="StartMenuShortcut" Guid="*">
          <Shortcut
              Id="ApplicationStartMenuShortcut"
              Name="SAP Ticket Checklist Assistant"
              Target="[INSTALLFOLDER]SAPTicketAssistant.exe"
              WorkingDirectory="INSTALLFOLDER" />
          <RemoveFolder Id="RemoveApplicationProgramsFolder" On="uninstall" />
          <RegistryValue
              Root="HKCU"
              Key="Software\YourOrganization\SAPTicketAssistant"
              Name="Installed"
              Type="integer"
              Value="1"
              KeyPath="yes" />
        </Component>
      </Directory>
    </StandardDirectory>

    <Feature Id="MainFeature" Title="SAP Ticket Checklist Assistant" Level="1">
      <ComponentRef Id="MainExecutable" />
      <ComponentRef Id="StartMenuShortcut" />
    </Feature>
  </Package>
</Wix>
```

Replace `PUT-A-STABLE-GUID-HERE` with a valid GUID and retain the same upgrade code for future versions of the same product family.

> MSI component design, install scope, shortcuts, registry keys, upgrade handling, and 32-bit versus 64-bit settings should be reviewed by the organization's application-packaging team.

### 15.4 Build output

The WiX build should produce a file similar to:

```text
SAPTicketAssistantSetup.msi
```

Place the final MSI directly in the release output location with its checksum and release notes.

