## 16. Creating an MSI with Advanced Installer

Advanced Installer provides a graphical workflow.

Typical process:

1. Create a new MSI project.
2. Set the product name to `SAP Ticket Checklist Assistant`.
3. Set the manufacturer and version.
4. Select the required install scope.
5. Add `dist\SAPTicketAssistant.exe` to the application folder.
6. Configure the application folder under Program Files.
7. Create a Start menu shortcut.
8. Optionally create a desktop shortcut.
9. Configure upgrades so that an older release is replaced.
10. Configure digital signing if a certificate is available.
11. Build the project.
12. Test installation, repair, upgrade, and uninstall on a clean machine.

Save the Advanced Installer project file in source control so that future releases use the same product configuration.

